cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this specification, please cite it using the metadata below. Specification text CC BY 4.0; schemas and examples EUPL-1.2 (see LICENSE)."
type: software
title: "L-euro: open protocol for digital entitlements (vouchers, coupons, tickets, discounts)"
version: "0.1.0-draft"
date-released: "2026-12-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/SolidarityLab/L-euro"
url: "https://github.com/SolidarityLab/L-euro"
abstract: >-
  L-euro defines a common data model, lifecycle and six separate roles
  (issuer, payer, holder, acceptor, depositary, cover custodian) for
  entitlements that are issued today as vouchers, coupons, tickets and
  discounts. The depositary is a dispatcher that keeps a register of
  pseudonymous holder accounts and events; it does not issue rights or
  identity attributes and does not hold the cover. Entitlements are not
  money. Draft for public comment.
keywords:
  - vouchers
  - entitlements
  - passkey
  - WebAuthn
  - EUDI Wallet
  - open protocol
  - public programmes
